{
  "_doc": "Oathwild's monsters and summoned companions. `art` = the body id in data/art.json (the art helper's fal.ai roster; `ready` bodies exist now, `waiting` ones are drawn and wait for fal credit). A row with `base` reuses a Farhold enemy/pet row (farhold/data/enemies.json `enemies` or `pets`) for its numbers, with `scale` multipliers on health/damage/xp/gold (Farhold's rows are level-1 numbers for monsters met deeper in its world, so Oathwild scales them to its two regions) and `set` fields laid over it. A row with `hp` is Oathwild's own. Levels come from the region and camp (regions.json); rpg.makeEnemy grows them per level (curves in combat.json `farholdEnemies`, then x combat.json `monsterScale`). No wisps (lessons rule 72). Wildlife round 2026-11-25 (owner: \"Where are all the wild life? The world still feels empty\"): Quaternius animals (data/critters.json). `temper`: hostile (default) hunts you; defensive never starts a fight but answers a blow; skittish never fights and runs from a hero closer than `fleeRange` (half that when you sneak). Every creature with nobody to fight wanders `wander` metres round its home (combat.json monsters.wanderDefault).",
